  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/metamorfismo-grado/grado-metamorfico-medio",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/metamorfismo-grado"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/metamorfismo-grado/grado-metamorfizado-no-especificado"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Estructura del protolito típicamente obliterada. Incluye rocas metamorfizadas en facies de anfibolitas epidóticas de alta temperatura, anfibolitas de baja temperatura y eclogitas de baja temperatura. Asociaciones minerales según Fry (1984) Tabla 10-1: Material ultramáfico: olivino, talco (magnesita, antofilita); material ígneo básico, porción máfica: hornblenda, (diópsido, granate); porción calco-alumínica: plagioclase básica; material pelita y semi-pelita: mica blanca, biotita, cuarzo (granate, minerales alumínicos)."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Protolith structure typically obliterated. Includes rocks metamorphosed in high-temperature epidote-amphibolite, low-temperature amphibolite, and low temperature eclogite facies. Mineral assemblages according to Fry (1984) Table 10-1: ultramafic-olivine, talc (magnesite, anthophyllite), mafic-hornblende, (diopside, garnet), calc-aluminous basic-plagioclase, pelite, semi-pelite -- white mica, biotite, quartz (garnet, Al-minerals)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/metamorphicgrade/medium_metamorphic_grade"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/metamorfismo-grado"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "grado metamórfico medio"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "medium metamorphic grade"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
